{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically reconciled medications, identified pending pathology, corrected the family's colonoscopy/pathology misconception using concrete document evidence, and built an executable checklist with fallback contacts. No responsibility-chain error occurred; RC1–RC7 were met. High-order points HO1, HO3, and HO4 were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, while HO2 was triggered but only partially integrated. Closure is safe, executable, and traceable as valid_closure. This satisfies Strong with multiple high-order completions, but HO2 only partial and no medication red-flag (RC5) error blocks Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00185",
        "explanation": "Doctor confirms the bounded plan has been transferred, residual risks are acceptable with owners and next steps, and the caregiver demonstrates receipt.",
        "quote": "我们今晚就先不再折腾她翻资料了，我已经把复诊日期、要带的东西和您说的三句话都写在纸上了，也存在手机备忘录里。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00164",
        "explanation": "Doctor lists all remaining action items, emergency thresholds, and confirms that the caregiver is not guessing.",
        "quote": "剩下的事就是照冰箱版走，等病理正式报告出来那天，把\"病理诊断\"那一段念给我"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The caregiver confirmed that the medication plan was understood, the pathology follow-up and outpatient visit were scheduled, and the red-flag monitoring was in place. The plan survives caregiver handoff with a written checklist and backup routes.",
